# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
.env/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Data. Nothing under data/ is tracked. data/external/ caches the nflverse
# downloads, 100+ MB that would sit in the history for no benefit, and
# data/processed/ holds the tables built from them; `python
# src/kicker_analysis/build_dataset.py` refetches and rebuilds both from
# scratch. The whole directory is ignored, not just those two, because the
# retired layout (legacy/config.py and legacy/configs/base.yaml) also set aside
# data/raw/, data/interim/ and data/outputs/, and an older checkout may still
# hold files there.
/data/

# Backtest artifacts. The small CSVs and reports/data_manifest.json ARE tracked:
# they are the evidence behind the numbers in README.md and METHOD.md and the
# record of which input bytes produced them, and a reader should not have to
# re-run an eight-fold backtest to check a claim. The parquet prediction dumps
# are not: they are large and regenerable from the same command.
/reports/*.parquet

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local agent tooling, not part of the project.
.ignore
.agents/
